target:    src/Migration/MigrationManager.php
gate:      composer test:migration-probe-query-budget
kind:      guard-removal
expect:    without consulting a transient first
rationale: Removes the cross-request cache from getOfferedMigrations(), leaving the per-request memo. That is the shape the defect actually had, and the memo makes it LOOK handled: within one request the two call sites -- registerPage() on admin_menu and the notice renderer on admin_notices -- cost one probe, so a test that only counts calls in a single request stays green. The cost is paid on EVERY admin page load instead, permanently: six information_schema.COLUMNS aggregates from ConvertTablesToUtf8mb4 plus two SHOW COLUMNS from AddUserAgentDimension, on a healthy install, forever -- because the release notes tell owners not to run the optional migrations. The guard is `!needsMigration() && [] === getOfferedMigrations()`, whose LEFT operand is a negation -- true exactly when nothing is owed -- so the right side runs precisely in the healthy steady state. (`&&` short-circuits normally; what costs is which side the negation puts first.)
---
--- a/src/Migration/MigrationManager.php
+++ b/src/Migration/MigrationManager.php
@@ -131,21 +131,10 @@
         // NOT keyed on migrationSetFingerprint(), deliberately, and it inherits the limitation
         // that buys: a migration ADDED by an update stays invisible until this expires, up to
         // PROBE_TTL. needsMigration()'s transient has exactly the same property, and keying only
         // one of the two would make them disagree about how fresh they are — a difference nothing
         // explains and the next reader takes for a bug. If it is worth closing, both move together.
-        $cached = get_transient(self::TRANSIENT_OFFERED);
-
-        if (is_array($cached)) {
-            $ids = array_flip($cached);
-
-            return $this->offeredMemo = array_filter(
-                $this->migrations,
-                static fn($migration) => $migration->isOptional() && isset($ids[$migration->getId()])
-            );
-        }
-
         $offered     = [];
         $unavailable = false;
 
         foreach ($this->migrations as $key => $migration) {
             if (!$migration->isOptional()) {
